    {
      "id": "claim_cf87134ed7c94e649431adfe1273945a",
      "statement": "Evidence routing is current-first and mandatory for named source paths and routed evidence-map files: BM25 runs over the benchmark's natural-language concept descriptions (never source syntax), selectors resolve deterministically to raw source, a named missing file receives the full tracked-file manifest, and larger corpora retain mandatory routed evidence plus a minimum eight-excerpt BM25 set within a soft budget.",
